or replacement procedures. NeuroPace, Inc. was incorporated in 1997 and is headquartered in Mountain View, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Joel D. Becker | CEO, President & Director | Age 57 | Compensation: $1.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 209 people. Revenue per employee of $478K ranks in the above the sector median among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 22%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $53K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Neuropace, Inc. is a micro-cap healthcare business with a $259M market cap on $100M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +30% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -201% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 74% confirm genuine pricing power.","The company is burning through $11M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -2.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 19.1% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and stock-based comp at 11% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 4.5% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-4.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 16% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 348% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"NeuroPace (NPCE) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/neuropace-npce-q3-2026-earnings-054351000.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794548994.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.459,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"What NeuroPace (NPCE) Said on Its Q3 Earnings Call","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/healthcare/articles/neuropace-npce-said-q3-earnings-041433417.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794543273.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.542,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"(NPCE) Movement as an Input in Quant Signal Sets","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/134/NPCE_Movement_as_an_Input_in_Quant_Signal_Sets_111226055801_1794524281.html","date":"2026-11